# Git Commit Rules

## No Cursor Co-Author

When making git commits, **do NOT include Cursor as a co-author**. Never use this format:

```bash
# ❌ NEVER DO THIS
git commit -m "message" --trailer "Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>"
```

## Correct Commit Format

Only the user should appear as the author:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
git commit -m "Your descriptive commit message"
```

## Git Config

Ensure the git configuration uses only the user's identity:

```bash
git config user.name "Your Name"
git config user.email "your.email@example.com"
```

**Important**: Do NOT set any git commit templates or aliases that include co-author trailers.

## Before Any Commit

1. Run `git log -1 --format='%an %ae'` to verify the commit author is correct
2. Check that no co-author trailers are being added
3. Confirm with the user before pushing to remote
